>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Data processing</div>
      <h1>Who does what with your data.</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 15 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose-section" style="padding-top:48px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          For the commerce and advertising data we read from your platforms, <b>you</b> decide what
          happens to it and <b>we</b> process it on your instructions to produce your reports. For
          the contact details you give us so we can run the engagement, we're responsible directly.
        </p>

        <h2>What we process, and why</h2>
        <p>
          We process your Shopify order, product and sales data and your Google and Meta ad-spend
          data, for the single purpose of producing your monthly reports. As set out in our
          <a href="/privacy">privacy</a> policy, we do not take your customers' names, emails, phone
          numbers or addresses — the software is built to leave that data behind.
        </p>

        <h2>How it's kept safe</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Access credentials are encrypted where they're stored.</li>
          <li>Each brand's data is isolated at the database level, enforced in the database itself.</li>
          <li>The access we hold is read-only — we can't change anything in your accounts.</li>
          <li>Access is limited to the analyst preparing your reports.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Sub-processors</h2>
        <p>
          To run the service we rely on a small number of providers. Each handles only what it needs
          to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <b>Our cloud hosting and database provider</b> — stores the data and runs the service.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Resend</b> — delivers report emails and notifications to you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Anthropic</b> — turns a report's already-computed figures into plain-English wording.
            Only the calculated numbers are sent; no customer personal data is involved because we
            hold none. This step can be switched off, in which case fixed templates are used instead.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Your source platforms — <b>Shopify</b>, <b>Google Ads</b> and <b>Meta</b> — are where your
          data originates; we only read from them.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it's processed</h2>
        <p>
          Data may be processed outside your own country by the providers above. Where that happens,
          it's on the basis those providers offer for international transfers.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep your data while your engagement is active, and delete it on request when you leave
          — your credentials are revoked and your orders, cost data, computed figures, reports and
          connection records are removed. See <a href="/privacy">privacy</a> for detail.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If we add or change a sub-processor, we'll update this page. Questions:
          <a href="mailto:hello@getgrossline.com">hello@getgrossline.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
